      "text": "Puneet Yadav\n\npuneety259@gmail.com | +919399336702 | linkedin | github | portfolio\n\nAbout me\nMERN stack developer with hands-on experience building scalable web applications and RESTful APIs. Completed\na 3-month software development internship at Sheryians Pvt. Ltd, where I worked with Node.js, Express.js, and\nMongoDB. Developed multiple full-stack projects, including an e-commerce platform with payment integration\nand an AI-powered chatbot. Seeking opportunities to contribute to innovative web development projects.\nTechnical Skills\n• Languages : JavaScript (ES6+)\n• Frontend : React.js, Next.js, HTML5, CSS3, Tailwind CSS, Bootstrap, Context API, Redux Toolkit\n• Backend : Node.js, Express.js, REST APIs, JWT, OAuth, GenAI APIs\n• Database : MongoDB, Mongoose, Aggregation, Indexing, localStorage\n• Tools : Git, GitHub, Postman, Vercel\nInternship\nSheryians Private Limited, Bhopal Full Stack Intern\nProject: Recruitment Website\n• Led end-to-end development of the Candidate Profile module across both frontend and backend, working closely\nwith the team through Git-based collaboration.\n• Integrated AI-driven resume parsing with automated redaction of personally identifiable information (PII) to\nmaintain data confidentiality.\n• Created secure APIs to support profile creation, modification, and controlled updates of personal details,\nadhering to clean workflow standards.\n• Built and improved frontend interfaces for profile management while engaging in active collaboration through\ncode reviews, pull requests, and version control.\nEducation\nSant Singaji Institute of Science and Management, Sandalpur\nB.A. in Computer Applications\n\nAug 2018 – June 2021\n\nProjects\nCricCart E-commerce Platform [Live Preview]\n• Built a full-stack e-commerce application using the MERN stack with JWT-based authentication.\n• Implemented complete product CRUD functionality managing 50+ products efficiently.\n• Integrated Razorpay payment gateway for secure online payments and real-time order processing.\n• Developed user cart functionality and a seller dashboard for seamless shopping and product management.\nFood Recipe Website [Live Preview]\n• Built a React-based recipe application with full CRUD functionality and favorite management.\n• Used Context API, React Router, and Tailwind CSS for state management and responsive UI.\n• Implemented localStorage for persistent data handling and smooth user experience.\nCertifications\nFull Stack MERN Development\nSheryians Coding School • Bhopal, MP • 2025\nDiploma in Software Development\nSant Singaji Institute of Science and Management • Sandalpur, Madhya Pradesh • 2024",
      "fontSize": 6.645105390343245,
